# Resources

Resources live in `:shared:common-resources/src/commonMain/moko-resources/`. The dedicated `:common-resources` module owns them and re-exports the generated `MR` accessor in package `dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.common.resources`.

## Layout

```
common-resources/src/commonMain/moko-resources/
  base/strings.xml          # default locale
  fonts/*.ttf               # custom typefaces
  images/*.png              # bundled chrome icons (positions, Radiant/Dire)
```

Basenames must be identifier-safe — moko mirrors them verbatim in the generated accessor:

- `NotoSans-Regular.ttf` → `MR.fonts.notosans_regular`

## Strings

`moko-resources/base/strings.xml`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<resources>
    <string name="all_heroes">All heroes</string>
    <string name="hero_filter">Hero filter</string>
</resources>
```

Usage:

```kotlin
import dev.icerock.moko.resources.compose.stringResource
import dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.common.resources.MR

Text(text = stringResource(MR.strings.all_heroes))
```

Naming: `{feature}_{element}_{description}` for feature-scoped strings; `{element}_{description}` for shared ones.

No hardcoded user-facing strings in composables. Logs and debug text are allowed inline.

## Fonts

Custom typefaces live in `moko-resources/fonts/`. `theme/Type.kt` (in `:shared:common-ui`) builds the `FontFamily` via `dev.icerock.moko.resources.compose.asFont`:

```kotlin
val regular = MR.fonts.notosans_regular.asFont(weight = FontWeight.Normal)
val bold = MR.fonts.notosans_bold.asFont(weight = FontWeight.Bold)
val family = FontFamily(listOfNotNull(regular, bold))
```

`asFont` is nullable on platforms that fail to load the typeface — fall back to `FontFamily.Default`.

## Images

App-chrome icons (position icons, Radiant/Dire squares) live in `moko-resources/images/` and render through `dev.icerock.moko.resources.compose.painterResource`:

```kotlin
import dev.icerock.moko.resources.compose.painterResource
import dev.nonoxy.d2buildhelper.common.resources.MR

Image(painter = painterResource(MR.images.position_1), contentDescription = null)
```

Image files **must** carry a moko scale suffix `@{n}x` — e.g. `position_1@1x.png`. Without it moko emits the `MR.images` accessor but no Android `drawable`, and the build fails with `Unresolved reference 'drawable'`. The accessor name strips the suffix (`position_1@1x.png` → `MR.images.position_1`).

Only bundle static app chrome here. Game-entity icons (heroes, items, abilities) come from the backend response (`iconUrl` field) — do not bundle them or construct Steam CDN URLs on the client. See `mobile-network.mdc`.
